        "Content": "Riverview House, Rushbrooke, Cobh, Co. Cork\r\n\r\nGuide Price: €1,500,000\r\n\r\nSet along the picturesque shoreline of Cork Harbour, Riverview House is an exceptional Victorian waterfront residence of remarkable character, history and elegance. Occupying a beautifully landscaped site extending to just under one acre, this distinguished red brick property enjoys uninterrupted panoramic views across the harbour towards Monkstown, boasting private water access for swimming, mooring and sailing, this remarkable coastal residence presents an increasingly rare opportunity to acquire an exceptional waterfront home.\r\nDating back to the mid-1800s, Riverview House forms part of an exclusive collection of Victorian villa-style residences constructed during the expansion of the Cork to Cobh railway line and the development of Queenstown as one of Ireland’s most important maritime destinations. Built in the fashionable red brick style of the Victorian era, the property stands today as a striking reminder of the architectural heritage associated with the golden age of rail and harbour expansion in Rushbrooke. \r\n\r\nBelieved to have originally served as a luxurious holiday villa overlooking what was once a fashionable waterfront retreat, Riverview House combines period grandeur with an enviable waterside lifestyle. The property has retained a wealth of original features throughout, including elegant sash windows, decorative panelling and its iconic red brick façade, all carefully preserved and presented in pristine condition.\r\nThe interior has been thoughtfully maintained to honour the home’s heritage while providing comfortable and refined living spaces suited to modern family life. The principal reception rooms, conservatory and kitchen are all positioned to maximise the spectacular harbour views, creating a seamless connection between the home and its breathtaking surroundings. From the ever-changing activity on the water to the peaceful coastal setting, Riverview House offers a truly unique living experience.\r\n\r\nThe accommodation within the main house comprises four generous bedrooms and two bathrooms together with a selection of elegant reception spaces including a formal dining room, living room, conservatory and kitchen, each enjoying an abundance of natural light and exceptional outlooks across Cork Harbour. The BER is a G and the BER No 119484855.\r\n\r\nThe Mews:\r\n\r\nAdding further appeal to the estate is the original Victorian coach house, now beautifully converted into a detached two-bedroom residence known as The Mews. Rich in character and history, this charming accommodation provides an ideal guest residence, extended family accommodation or private retreat. The Mews comprises a spacious kitchen and dining area, living room, two bedrooms and two bathrooms.\r\nExternally, the grounds are beautifully landscaped and exceptionally private, with mature planting, expansive lawns and a private garage enhancing the overall setting. A standout feature of the property is its private water access, a rare and highly desirable addition that further elevates the exclusivity of this remarkable home. The Mews is 98 sq m and has a BER of B. Ber No is 119485159. \r\n\r\nRiverview House has enjoyed front-row views to some of Cork Harbour’s most iconic events over the years, including the Tall Ships and the famous Cork to Cobh yacht race, further reflecting its unique position within one of Ireland’s most celebrated natural harbours. This is a rare opportunity to acquire a landmark waterfront residence of exceptional charm, heritage and prestige in an unrivalled coastal location.\r\n\r\nProperty Features:\r\n\r\n•\tExceptional Victorian red brick waterfront residence \r\nSet on just under one acre of landscaped grounds \r\n•\tPrivate water access to Cork Harbour \r\n•\tPanoramic harbour views towards Monkstown \r\n•\tFour-bedroom main residence \r\n•\tDetached two-bedroom coach house residence known as The Mews \r\n•\tOriginal sash windows and decorative panelling - restored\r\n•\tElegant period features retained throughout \r\n•\tNew roof and fascia \r\n•\tConservatory overlooking the harbour \r\n•\tOil central heating \r\n•\tPrivate garage \r\n•\tMature landscaped gardens \r\n•\tElectric gates \r\n•\tFreehold property \r\n•\tMains water and mains sewerage \r\n•\tPrime waterfront setting in Rushbrooke, Cobh \r\n•\t207 sq m"
      },
